<p>I'm speechless: Copilot get this well understood, old problem with a
well established, extensively documented platform all wrong. My
question was:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Can you write UTF-8 in your Java .properties file?"</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And it said:
<img
  class="centered"
  src="/graphics/2026/copilot-utf8-properties.png"
  alt="Copilot wrongly answering how to read UTF-8 from a Java .properties file"
/></p>
<p>Its answer has three problems:</p>
<ol>
<li>The test data can be written with ISO-8859-1 encoding, so it
   doesn't prove that UTF-8 is working.</li>
<li>What's worse, it doesn't work.</li>
<li>Lastly, it gives the impression that this used to be a problem, but
   is no longer, listing different Java versions and so on, adding
   credibility to its answer. But alas, it doesn't work. You have to
   recode the string, read the bytes as ISO 8859-1, and then construct
   a new string as UTF-8.</li>
</ol>
<p>SMH.</p>
